==Strategy==
In this stage, Bun Bun Symbiote is the biggest threat, since his [[Wave Attack]]s can devastate entire stacks of crowd-controllers and even hit your backliners. Therefore, it's advised to bring a [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shield]] to stop his waves from hitting your stack, [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] being the best choice. [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]], if he has a decently leveled Freeze [[Talents|Talent]], can permafreeze Bun Bun Symbiote, negating this need for a Wave Shield to protect against Symbiote's Waves, while also providing decent DPS. [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]] and [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] are also great in this stage, although again, one unlucky Wave can take out your entire stack.

A hyper-boosted Cameraman Cat is recommended when revisiting this stage for {{4c}}.

==='''Strategy 1 ([[Cheese]])'''===
If you have [[Li'l Tank Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Wall Cat]], this stage can be easily won without having to fight the Bun Buns at all. Simply send a couple of Li'l Walls out at the beginning and wait for them to reach the enemy base and begin damaging it. (You may want to fire the [[Cat Cannon]] to clear out enemy peons to make the first part faster.) They will damage the base so slowly that peons will back up behind the base until the enemy limit is reached so that Teacher Bun Bun and the others will be unable to spawn. After enough enemies are stacked up behind the base, simply begin spamming Li'l Wall and/or [[Li'l Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Cat]] to slowly wear the enemy base down. To speed it up, you may also want to send units with higher DPS like [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Artist Cat]] and [[Axe Cat (Normal Cat)|Dark Cat]] once all the peons are behind the base.

Bringing any attacker without piercing attacks will greatly help once the enemy limit is reached.

